    "narrative": "The Austin Waves' offense is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.47), both of whom present must-start profiles. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive +17% boost due to a soft matchup against Martinez, and his elevated spot in the order maximizes his run-production potential. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages a favorable platoon advantage against Rod\u00f3n, with his score climbing significantly due to a +8% bump for batting second. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) remains a critical focus for our scarcity-driven strategy; while his matchup against Ober is challenging, his elite sprint speed and a +2% efficiency boost derived from the pitcher's slow delivery make him our highest-upside play for stolen base opportunities today.\n\nStrategic platoon edges and environmental factors are shifting several mid-tier scores into viable start territory. **Luis Robert Jr.** (66.44) is a prime beneficiary of these dynamics, gaining +14% from a lefty-heavy platoon advantage and a +5% boost from winds blowing out. **Coby Mayo** (63.53) also looks strong despite a -8% platoon drag, as the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a weak opposing arm in Martinez keeps his floor high. Conversely, **Kyle Tucker** (58.73) underperforms his typical elite status due to a sub-optimal matchup against Bachar, though he remains an essential hold.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Miguel Vargas** (47.01), who hovered on the edge of the active lineup throughout the morning. While **Miguel Vargas** boasts a strong xwOBA of 0.387 and a positive wind-assisted park factor, the proximity to a tough matchup against McLean\u2014combined with the superior daily efficiency scores of our active middle infielders\u2014ultimately relegated him to the bench. We continue to monitor the status of **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Jung**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Luis Lara** for future rotation; meanwhile, the ongoing absences of **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** remain the primary constraints on our depth as we navigate the home stretch.",
